          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is known as the
            %em prime geodesic theorem
            is a result that descrives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic"} asymptotic
            distribution of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+geodesics"} prime geodesics
            on a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+manifold"} hyperbolic manifold
          %p
            The prime geodesic theorem is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogy"} analogous
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number+theorem"} prime number theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+zeta+function"} Riemann zeta function
            control the error term in the prime number theorem, so the zeros of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Selberg+zeta+function"} Selberg zeta function
            control the error term in the prime geodesic theorem.
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+manifold"} hyperbolic manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d + 1
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Gamma \coloneqq \pi_1(X)
          %p
            be its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
          %p
            For each element
            %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \in \Gamma
            there exists one closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
            in
            %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            representing it. By standard convenient abuse of notation we write
            %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            also for that geodesic. Write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l(\gamma)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/length"} length
                of the geodesic
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            %li
              %p
                %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %mi l
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\gamma) \coloneqq e^{l(\gamma)}
                for what is called its
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em norm
            %li
              %p
                %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\Gamma(x)
                for the number of primitive elements
                %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \in \Gamma
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\gamma) \leq x
          %p
            The
            %em prime geodesic theorem
            is a statement of the form that this number
            %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\Gamma(x)
            satisfies
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi li
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mi N
                  %mi li
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi error
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi term
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_\Gamma(x)
                  \=
                  li(x^d)
                  +
                  \\underoverset{n = 0}{N}{\sum} li(x^{s_n}) + (error\;term)
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi li
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %munderover
                        %mo ∫
                        %mn 0
                        %mi x
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mi t
                        %mrow
                          %mi ln
                          %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} li(x) = \underoverset{0}{x}{\int}\frac{d t}{ln t}
                is the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithmic+integral+function"} logarithmic integral function
            %li
              %p
                %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{s_1, \cdots, s_N\}
                are the zeros of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Selberg+zeta+function"} Selberg zeta function
                in the interval
                %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d/2,d)
            %li
              %p
                %math#mathml_613e7f1ba6d03ea9f2594da07128eb8fe37f79b6_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi error
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi term
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (error\;term)
                is some term, estimates of which are the main content of this class of theorems.
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original estimates are due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atle+Selberg"} Atle Selberg
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Sarnak"} Peter Sarnak
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Sarnak"}> Peter Sarnak
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Prime Geodesic Theorems
          %p Further developments include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Koyama
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Prime geodesic theorem for arithmetic compact surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://imrn.oxfordjournals.org/content/1998/8/383.extract"} web
            %li
              %p
                Maki Nakasuji,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Prime Geodesic Theorem for Higher-Dimensional Hyperbolic Manifold
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/3845331"} JSTOR
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/tran/2006-358-08/S0002-9947-06-04122-5/S0002-9947-06-04122-5.pdf"} pdf
            %li#SoundararajanYoung13
              %p
                K. Soundararajan, Matthew P. Young,
                = succeed ",J." do
                  %em The Prime Geodesic Theorem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.5486"} arXiv:1011.5486
          %p Discussion for the case of simple geodesics in hyperbolic surfaces contains
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Rivin"}> Igor Rivin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Simple Curves on Surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://link.springer.com/article/10.1023%2FA%3A1012010721583"} web
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maryam+Mirzakhani"}> Maryam Mirzakhani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Growth of the number of simple closed geodesics on hyperbolic surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://annals.math.princeton.edu/2008/168-1/p03"} web
